- Identify the 10 most abundant genera across all samples.
- Group all remaining genera (including ASVs with no genus) into an "Other" category.
- Create a stacked bar plot showing genus relative abundance for each sample.
- As in Section 7, make one version faceted by `Location` and one by `Type`.
- Include appropriate axis labels, a legend title, and `theme_classic()`.
- Rotate the sample labels on the x-axis so they are easier to read.

Hint: as for Section 7.

